By default, ollama uses user "ollama", group "ollama" and a directory
$LOCALSTATEDIR/lib/ollama. To make sure everything works, do these
steps after installing the package (adjust $LOCALSTATEDIR according to
your $_PREFIX).

1. Create group and user "ollama":
  groupadd -g 393 -r ollama
  useradd -r -u 393 -g ollama -d $LOCALSTATEDIR/lib/ollama -s /sbin/nologin -c "Ollama service account" ollama

2. Create the models directory and set permissions:
  mkdir -p $LOCALSTATEDIR/lib/ollama/models
  chown -R ollama:ollama $LOCALSTATEDIR/lib/ollama
  chmod 750 $LOCALSTATEDIR/lib/ollama

3. Create the log file:
  touch $LOCALSTATEDIR/log/ollama.log
  chown ollama:ollama $LOCALSTATEDIR/log/ollama.log

To start ollama at boot and stop it properly at shutdown, make sure
rc.local and rc.local_shutdown contain the following lines
(adjust $SYSCONFDIR according to your $_PREFIX):

  /etc/rc.d/rc.local
  ==================
  # Start ollama
  if [ -x $SYSCONFDIR/rc.d/rc.ollama ]; then
    $SYSCONFDIR/rc.d/rc.ollama start
  fi

  /etc/rc.d/rc.local_shutdown
  ===========================
  # Stop ollama
  if [ -x $SYSCONFDIR/rc.d/rc.ollama ]; then
    $SYSCONFDIR/rc.d/rc.ollama stop
  fi
